          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "pearls": [
      "Amyloidosis is the classic cause: a low-voltage ECG with thick ventricular walls on echo.",
      "In cardiac amyloidosis, avoid non-dihydropyridine calcium channel blockers and use digoxin only with caution, because they bind the fibrils and cause toxicity.",
      "Kussmaul sign, a rise in JVP on inspiration, occurs in both restrictive cardiomyopathy and constrictive pericarditis."
    ],
